% Verified 2026-08-24 by direct fetch of arxiv.org/html/2509.23202 and,
% for the MXFP scale-fitting claim below, by downloading and extracting
% text from the paper's own PDF (arxiv.org/pdf/2509.23202) since the
% relevant appendix was not rendered by the HTML fetch.
% Supports scoop-risk differentiation on BOTH stated grounds. Confirmed
% verbatim: "The per-element MSE: MSE(G) := E[(X1-X1_hat)^2]" (Definition
% 3, Sec. 3, "Quantization Metrics"); "We assume that the 'native' weights
% and activations follow the Laplace distribution W ~ Laplace(0,b)..."
% (Definition 1, Sec. 3, "Modeling"). Both differ from this project's
% own metric (backward error) and operand model (t-Student), as claimed.
% ALSO supports SPEC.md's three-conventions rounding note (Step 6.1):
% confirmed verbatim in Appendix H ("MXFP SCALE FITTING"), Eq. (1):
% "s_E8M0 = (4/3) * 2^clamp(round(log2 s), -128, 127)", introduced as
% "The original MXFP quantization grid, with 4/3 re-scaling, quantizes
% scales as follows"; and separately, "we multiply the scale by 4/3
% following [52], which yields an unbiased estimate of the original scale
% and reduces quantization error" (Sec. 3/Appendix C), where reference
% [52] in this paper's own bibliography is confirmed to be
% `tseng2025training` below. Author list and ICLR 2026 status confirmed
% against arXiv/HuggingFace/dblp listings.
@inproceedings{egiazarian2026bridging,
